Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:28.530 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  talking ship all hand darken ship the  smoking lamp is out of object the  sickbay presents special problems in the  evening blue jackets plunged into  inactivity because they are sick or  injured grow restless during the long  days in their bunks days are long nights  longer still what can be done to ease  the tension to help the men relax till  they'll rest and sleep better  this man is tired of lying in his funk  tired physically tired mental when  you're sick the simple act of washing  your face and your hands and brushing  your teeth is refreshing and so evening  care begins with passing out the  necessary gear patients who cannot take  care of themselves are given healthy  choice  another valuable part of the evening  routine requires only a pair of trained  hands a little rubbing alcohol and a  towel a good back rub stimulates  circulation relaxes tired muscles  relieves fatigue give the patient as  much privacy as possible loosen his  clothing and turn him over on his side  or abdomen whichever is more comfortable  uncover the entire back place a towel on  the bed  or a little alcohol into your hands and  rub the back use the heels of the hands  and the fingers and rub with a firm  circular motion start at the shoulders  work slowly down the back gently but  firmly rubbing away the fatigue rubbing  away the tension go all the way down as  you rub you have a good opportunity to  observe the condition of his skin and to  be on the lookout for the reddened areas  which indicate the beginning of pressure  sores they may appear at any place where  bones come close to the surface of the  skin for instance here at the shoulder  blades or down here at the base of the  spine  when pressure sores first appear they  look like this just a red and skin area  they can usually be prevented if you rub  the danger spots frequently keep the bed  linen smooth and dry change the  patient's from one position to another  frequently so he doesn't fly on the sore  area it's neglected the skin breaks  becomes ulcerated and looks like this  finish the back rub with long firm  strokes keep your eyes open for those  reddened areas which mean the beginning  of trouble take a good look at the tips  of the shoulders at the elbows and at  the ears other likely spots are the hip  areas the outer side of the ankle and  the heels and at the knees the patient  has been well cared for and he's alright  just before you leave the crumbs are  swept out and wrinkles smoothed out  thoroughly the hospital corpsman knows  that these details are just as important  as the alcohol run the bunk is clean and  smooth and tight the alcohol rub has  stimulated his circulation and relaxed  you can see the response in his whole  attitude to care and consideration  quitting okay okay all right get some  homework for you  um not bad  beyond this welcome routine care there  may be some additional care required by  each individual patient when you're  finished all patients should be relaxed  comfortable and at ease mentally and  physically the patients come first as  they always do any unusual conditions  are reported to the medical officer then  the records which must be completed  before the ward is secured and you're  ready to be released  the senior hospital corpsman reports  today's activities to the Night Watch  and transfers to them the responsibility  of continuing the care of the patient  then the daywatch can shove off  the Nightman muster the patients and  check on their general condition they  should see that each one has been  attended to before the standing lights  are turned on at 2100  [Music]  during the long night watch especially  for the initially ill patient at least  once every hour a check is made on all  the patients to see that they're safe  and comfortable that all is secure  [Music]

